{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Make it happen, please, before me today.</b> Some say that he asked that HaShem arrange for him a distinguished young woman whose way it was never to go out at all, and that just now, by chance, she should come out before him specifically, so that she not be one of those who go out freely. Therefore the Torah says, ״וְאִישׁ לֹא יְדָעָהּ״ (Genesis 24:16) — no person knew her, for she had never gone out of the house except this one time. And therefore he needed to ask her, ״בַּת מִי אַתְּ״ (Genesis 24:23), and why did he not ask the other young women who were there? For without doubt she did not go alone; but because ״אִישׁ לֹא יְדָעָהּ״ — that is to say, no one recognized her."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:29:38.854091860Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}